          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21060 utils: add client jobstats selectors",
        "message": "LU-21060 utils: add client jobstats selectors\n\n- lljobstat has no OSC or MDC selector and does not know several\n  client metadata counters.\n- A record with only byte counters leaves the operation total unset.\n- Add -O/--osc and -M/--mdc, recognize the client operation names,\n  and set the operation total for byte-only records.\n- Extend sanity test_850: check both selector forms against an lctl\n  fixture, and saved, empty and invalid input. It skips when PyYAML\n  is missing, and accepts ENOENT from lctl on a node without any\n  job_stats file.\n- Also fix the program name in the lljobstat(8) SYNOPSIS.\n- The kernel interfaces follow in the next LU-21060 patch.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=850\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Krause <akrause@nvidia.com>\nChange-Id: Icb9093c3e0d4d8b45a82bb4916d9695b0d63b07d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
